```python
else:
    t, pred, commit = check_sigstore(path, chain[seq - 1][1], a.repo, 
a.workflow, a.ref)
    if not isinstance(pred, dict) or not isinstance(pred.get("from_seq"), int) 
or pred.get("to_seq") != seq \
            or not 1 <= pred["from_seq"] <= seq or pred != 
range_predicate(chain, pred["from_seq"], seq):
        raise Bad(f"anchors/{n}: attested range {pred!r} doesn't match this 
chain")
    ranges.append((pred["from_seq"], seq, commit))
    rows.append({"anchor": n, "kind": "sigstore", "entries": 
f"{pred['from_seq']}-{seq}", "existed_by": iso(t),
                 "writer_commit": commit})
    sigstore_seqs.add(seq)
except Bad as ex:
    bad.append(str(ex))
except CantCheck as ex:
    cant.append(f"anchors/{n}: {ex}")
```

When `check_sigstore` throws a `CantCheck` exception (because sigstore-python 
isn't installed), the `sigstore_seqs.add(seq)` line is never executed. That's 
why the missing .ots check doesn't trigger.

